      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"pair_id\": \"Khnemet|705752\", \"verdict\": \"different_name\", \"reasoning\": \"Record 2 reads as the signs ẖ, n, m, w, ꜥ, n, ḫ, w, in two elements (ẖnm.w and ꜥnḫ.w). In Khnemet, 'kh' matches ẖ, 'n' matches n and 'm' matches m. The w can be left out. The 'e' vowels could stand for ꜥ, but the second element needs an n and a ḫ (kh) after it, and the name has no letters for them. The final 't' also has no sign in the transliteration. It is not a feminine ending, because the transliteration has no t, and the t is not element-final in any element of record 2. So the signs n and ḫ of the second element are unmatched, and record 1 has a leftover consonant t. The names are different.\"}"
     }
